{"ref":"BDB, חִיצוֹן","hw":"חִיצוֹן","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">חִיצוֹן</span></big>  <strong>adj. outer, external</strong> (opp. <span dir=\"rtl\">פְּנִימִי</span>) f. <span dir=\"rtl\">חִיצוֹנָה</span> <strong>(</strong>for <span dir=\"rtl\">חוֹצוֹן</span>, by dissim., Ba<sup>NB xxix</sup> Phil<sup>BAS ii. 2. 362</sup> Ges<sup>§ 27. 3 R 6</sup><strong>)</strong>—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <a data-ref=\"II Kings 16:18\" href=\"/II_Kings.16.18\">2 K 16:18</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">מְבוֹא הַמֶּלֶךְ הַחִיצוֹנָה</span> the <em>outer</em> entry of the king (viz. to the Temple), <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 44:1\" href=\"/Ezekiel.44.1\">Ez 44:1</a> the <em>outer</em> gate of the sanctuary, <span dir=\"rtl\">החצר החיצונה</span> the <em>outer</em> court (of the Temple) <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 10:5\" href=\"/Ezekiel.10.5\">Ez 10:5</a> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 40:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.40.17\">40:17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 40:20\" href=\"/Ezekiel.40.20\">20</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 40:31\" href=\"/Ezekiel.40.31\">31</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 40:34\" href=\"/Ezekiel.40.34\">34</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 40:37\" href=\"/Ezekiel.40.37\">37</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 42:1\" href=\"/Ezekiel.42.1\">42:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 42:3\" href=\"/Ezekiel.42.3\">3</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 42:7\" href=\"/Ezekiel.42.7\">7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 42:8\" href=\"/Ezekiel.42.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 42:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.42.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 42:14\" href=\"/Ezekiel.42.14\">14</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 44:19\" href=\"/Ezekiel.44.19\">44:19</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 44:1\" href=\"/Ezekiel.44.1\">1</a>; <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 46:9\" href=\"/Ezekiel.46.9\">46:9</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 46:20\" href=\"/Ezekiel.46.20\">20</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 46:21\" href=\"/Ezekiel.46.21\">21</a>, cf. <a data-ref=\"Esther 6:4\" href=\"/Esther.6.4\">Est 6:4</a> (of Ahasuerus’ palace), <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 33:14\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.33.14\">2 Ch 33:14</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">חוֹמָה ח׳</span> an <em>outer</em> wall (built by Manasseh for the <span dir=\"rtl\">עִיר דָּוִיד</span>); <span dir=\"rtl\">הַחִיצוֹן</span> absol., in <span dir=\"rtl\">לַחִיצוֹן</span> <a data-ref=\"I Kings 6:29\" href=\"/I_Kings.6.29\">1 K 6:29</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Kings 6:30\" href=\"/I_Kings.6.30\">30</a>, <span dir=\"rtl\">בַּחִיצוֹן</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 41:17\" href=\"/Ezekiel.41.17\">Ez 41:17</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">הַבַּיִת</span> being understood) of the <em>outer</em> (part of the Temple), i.e. the Holy Place (cf. <a data-ref=\"BDB, פְּנִימִי\" href=\"/BDB,_פְּנִימִי\", dir=\"rtl\">פְּנִימִי</a>, <a data-ref=\"BDB, פְּנִ֫ימָה\" href=\"/BDB,_פְּנִ֫ימָה\", dir=\"rtl\">פְּנִימָה</a>, of the Holy of holies).<br><strong>2.</strong>  fig. <em>outward, external</em> <span dir=\"rtl\">הַמְּלָאבָה הַחִיצוֹנָה</span> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 11:16\" href=\"/Nehemiah.11.16\">Ne 11:16</a> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 26:29\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.26.29\">1 Ch 26:29</a>, of business not distinctively sacred, in which Levites were engaged (cf. the NH use of <span dir=\"rtl\">ח׳</span> to denote <em>extra-canonical</em>, as <em>Sanh.</em> 10:1 [Jost, 11:1 Surenh.] <span dir=\"rtl\">ספרים החיצונים</span>).","next":"BDB, חוץ²","prev":"BDB, חוּץ"}